0..47 Comment "/// Motives whose fixed endpoints reduce alike."
48..51 Comment "///"
52..125 Comment "/// Two transports along one path compare by their motives, then by their"
126..206 Comment "/// operands. Here the motives\' fixed endpoints differ as written and agree once"
207..283 Comment "/// they reduce. One endpoint calls a definition returning its argument. One"
284..361 Comment "/// transports along a reflexivity. One composes a path with a reflexivity on"
362..376 Comment "/// the right."
377..380 Comment "///"
381..457 Comment "/// The checker enters each written call against what the other motive holds"
458..533 Comment "/// there. The kernel reads the motives\' endpoints by its own reduction and"
534..545 Comment "/// agrees."
546..549 Comment "///"
550..654 Comment "/// - see: #4179 — the checker refused transports whose motives\' fixed endpoints differ by a reduction"
656..715 Comment "/// The identity on a type, a definition a motive may call."
